                "xpath": "/html[1]/body[1]/div[4]/div[2]/div[1]/div[12]/div[3]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]/div[1]",
                "asynchronous_ai_overview": false,
                "markdown": "![Learning the Hebrew letter Hey in Psalm 119](https://api.dataforseo.com/cdn/i/10110522-2762-0139-0000-33b7bdec8f62:4)\nThe Hebrew letter **He** (also spelled **Hei** or **Hey** , written as **ה** ) is the fifth letter of the [Hebrew Alphabet](https://hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Hey/hey.html).[[1]](https://hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Hey/hey.html)[[2]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137077/jewish/Heh.htm)\n\n### Core Facts\n\n- **Numeric Value:** 5 (used in gematria).\n- **Sound:** Makes an \"h\" sound (like in \"heaven\") at the beginning or middle of a syllable, and is often silent at the end of a word.\n- **Grammar Function:** Acts as the definite article prefix meaning \"the\" (e.g., *HaShem* ), a question prefix, or a directional suffix.\n- **Sacred Meaning:** Appears twice in the Tetragrammaton (the four-letter name of God, **יהוה** - Yod-He-Vav-He).[[1]](https://hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Hey/hey.html)[[2]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137077/jewish/Heh.htm)[[3]](https://dinahoverlien.com/2020/05/06/he/)[[4]](https://kriakala.com/hebrew-letter-he)[[5]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/He_(letter))[[6]](https://ephraimintheland.wordpress.com/2018/01/04/hey-%D7%94-the-breath-of-yhvh/)[[7]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZdYOBnPQdxo&t=532)\n\n### Symbolism & History\n\n- **Pictograph Origin:** Originally depicted a person with raised arms in wonder or a window, meaning \"behold,\" \"look,\" or \"breath/sigh\".\n- **Design:** Formed with a gap/opening at the bottom-left, which Jewish tradition interprets as a gateway for repentance and humility (resembling *matzah* rather than puffed-up leaven).\n- **Ancestry:** Served as the ancestor to the Greek **Epsilon** and the Latin **E**.[[1]](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/He_(letter))[[2]](https://hebrew4christians.com/Grammar/Unit_One/Aleph-Bet/Hey/hey.html)[[3]](https://www.chabad.org/library/article_cdo/aid/137077/jewish/Heh.htm)[[4]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HCqCc96LClE)\n\nWould you like to explore how He functions as a **prefix in Hebrew grammar** , or look into its **gematria and mystical symbolism** further?",
